# Commands run by scripts/quality-gate.sh. Each is run with `bash -c`.
# The gate has two tiers:
#   fast (default)  lint, typecheck, unit, acceptance, hardening, coverage, CRAP, acceptance locks
#   full            fast + mutation testing + hardening locks
# Required in fast (the gate FAILS if empty): LINT_CMD, UNIT_TEST_CMD, ACCEPTANCE_TEST_CMD,
#                                             DEPS_CMD
# Required in full (additionally):            MUTATION_CMD
# Optional (skipped if empty): TYPECHECK_CMD, HARDENING_TEST_CMD, COVERAGE_CMD, CRAP_CMD
# Each command must exit non-zero on failure. Thresholds belong inside the commands.

LINT_CMD="npx eslint ."
TYPECHECK_CMD="npx tsc --noEmit"
# Structural rules: layering, the core/shell boundary, cycles, orphans. Required in both tiers
# -- a layering violation is as much a defect as a failing test, and catching it in the
# implementer's fast loop is the whole point. Rules live in .dependency-cruiser.cjs (human-owned).
DEPS_CMD="npx depcruise src tests --config .dependency-cruiser.cjs"
UNIT_TEST_CMD="npx vitest run tests/unit"
ACCEPTANCE_TEST_CMD="npx vitest run tests/acceptance"
# Hardening tests (written by the hardener to kill mutants) run in BOTH tiers, so the
# implementer finds out immediately when a change breaks one. --passWithNoTests keeps the
# gate green before any hardening test exists.
HARDENING_TEST_CMD="npx vitest run tests/hardening --passWithNoTests"
COVERAGE_CMD="npx vitest run --coverage --coverage.thresholds.lines=80"
CRAP_CMD="python3 scripts/crap.py --max 8"
# Mutation testing. Full tier only; required there. Thresholds live in stryker.config.json
# (break: 75) -- Stryker exits non-zero when the score falls below the break threshold.
MUTATION_CMD="npx stryker run"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Examples (uncomment and adapt one block):
#
# TypeScript / Node
# LINT_CMD="npx eslint ."
# TYPECHECK_CMD="npx tsc --noEmit"
# DEPS_CMD="npx depcruise src tests --config .dependency-cruiser.cjs"
# UNIT_TEST_CMD="npx vitest run tests/unit"
# ACCEPTANCE_TEST_CMD="npx vitest run tests/acceptance"
# HARDENING_TEST_CMD="npx vitest run tests/hardening --passWithNoTests"
# COVERAGE_CMD="npx vitest run --coverage --coverage.thresholds.lines=80"
# MUTATION_CMD="npx stryker run"
#
# Python
# LINT_CMD="ruff check ."
# TYPECHECK_CMD="mypy src"
# DEPS_CMD="import-linter --config .importlinter"
# UNIT_TEST_CMD="pytest tests/unit -q"
# ACCEPTANCE_TEST_CMD="pytest tests/acceptance -q"
# COVERAGE_CMD="pytest --cov=src --cov-fail-under=80 -q"
#
# CRAP score = complexity^2 * (1 - coverage)^3 + complexity, per function.
# PHP:  PHPUnit can emit a crap4j report (--coverage-crap4j).
# Java: crap4j-style reports from coverage tooling.
# Other stacks: combine a complexity tool (e.g. `lizard`, multi-language) with your coverage
# report in a small script, e.g. CRAP_CMD="python3 scripts/crap.py --max 8"
# (ask Claude to write scripts/crap.py for your stack).
#
# Mutation testing (required in the full tier). StrykerJS covers JS/TS; other stacks have
# equivalents (mutmut or cosmic-ray for Python, PIT for Java, infection for PHP, cargo-mutants
# for Rust). The command must exit non-zero when the score falls below your break threshold.
# MUTATION_CMD="npx stryker run"
# MUTATION_CMD="mutmut run"
